# Eloquent query style

Use **normal Eloquent entry points** on models. Start chains from the model, not from a generic query builder unless necessary.

## Prefer

```php
User::where('active', true)->latest()->get();

$user->posts()->where('published', true)->get();

Course::findOrFail($id);
```

## Avoid unless justified

```php
User::query()->where('active', true)->get();
```

Use `Model::query()` only when you need an **explicit builder** for a complex chain that cannot start on the model (e.g. shared scope wiring, union/subquery builder passed between services). Add a brief comment explaining why.

## Also avoid when a model API exists

- `DB::table('users')` for domain data that has an Eloquent model — use the model instead
- Raw query builder in controllers when a relationship or scope on the model is clearer
